WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.960 line:10%
Imagine I invented a lamp that

2
00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:05.240 line:10%
turns away when I open

3
00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:06.200 line:10%
my work chat at night.

4
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.029 line:10%
You’re like, “I’ll just take

5
00:00:08.029 --> 00:00:08.427 line:10%
a quick peek.”

6
00:00:08.433 --> 00:00:10.555 line:10%
It’s already facing the wall.
Fun, right?

7
00:00:10.555 --> 00:00:13.915 line:10%
I throw the idea at an AI.
It immediately goes:

8
00:00:13.915 --> 00:00:16.675 line:10%
“Great! Audience, price,
subscription.

9
00:00:16.675 --> 00:00:19.315 line:10%
We launch on Friday.” Hold on.
All I’ve invented so far

10
00:00:19.315 --> 00:00:21.595 line:10%
is a sulking lamp.
Where did Friday

11
00:00:21.595 --> 00:00:23.955 line:10%
come from? I haven’t even decided

12
00:00:23.955 --> 00:00:26.355 line:10%
if it needs an “okay,
five more minutes” button.

13
00:00:26.355 --> 00:00:29.155 line:10%
And we already have
a lighting subscription. I say:

14
00:00:29.155 --> 00:00:31.035 line:10%
“Let’s just imagine

15
00:00:31.035 --> 00:00:33.475 line:10%
how it turns for now.”
The reply: “Of course.

16
00:00:33.475 --> 00:00:35.955 line:10%
Let’s start with a technical spec.”

17
00:00:35.955 --> 00:00:38.635 line:10%
One question would be enough:
are we dreaming,

18
00:00:38.635 --> 00:00:41.755 line:10%
or are we getting started?
Okay, I’m showing the lamp our plan.

19
00:00:41.755 --> 00:00:44.355 line:10%
There. It turned away again.
